Z||000004||fiero56||01-09-2001||01:58 PM||||Sounds like you are converting from auto to manual?<P>I wouldn't go for it unless you are set on doing the conversion. Plus, you have to make sure a Getrag is what you want. Unless you already have, I suggest driving one of them before deciding you want one. It might change your mind...it's changed mine.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||01-09-2001||02:25 PM||||What year is the Fiero that you are putting the Getrag into?<P>I have pretty much everything needed to do the conversion......it's all from an '88 Formula.<P>LMK.||||reg||10
Z||000006||Will||01-09-2001||05:07 PM||||I checked. <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  also has the transmission mount brackets.<P>Why do I hear bad things about the Getrag?<BR>I drove my recently purchased '87 GT for a few weeks with whatever oil was in it when I bought it. I admit that the transmission was somewhat reluctant.<P>However, on both my '87 GT and my '86 SE I am currently using ATF instead of gear oil or synchromesh fluid. Both shift very easily, very smoothly, and very fast without working hard at it.<P>I don't see why people complain about Getrags.<P>I will admit that I have never driven and Isuzu equipped car.||||reg||1
